---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config/site";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../lib/schema";
import family from "../assets/images/about-us.jpg";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "About", path: "/about/" },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Weld Creations | Third-Generation Welder"
  description="Weld Creations is a family-owned precision welding and fabrication shop in Glendora, CA, run by third-generation welder Mark May. AWS D17.1 certified."
  ogImage={family}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
      <h1>About Weld Creations</h1>
      <p class="lead">A family-owned precision welding and fabrication shop in Glendora, run by third-generation welder {SITE.owner}.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="container">
    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        Weld Creations builds the welded parts and equipment that manufacturers depend on: sanitary stainless for pharmaceutical and food production,
        precision TIG welding in stainless, aluminum, titanium and nickel alloys, and repeatable production runs. We're a family business, and we treat
        every part like our name is on it, because it is.
      </p>

      <h2>A third-generation welder</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.owner} is a third-generation welder. The trade was passed down, and so were the standards: a weld is either right or it isn't.
        That shows up in the details engineers notice, such as consistent bead profiles across a production run, clean back-purged roots on
        sanitary tube, and machined features that stay in position after welding.
      </p>
      <p>
        Mark is certified to <strong>AWS D17.1</strong>, the American Welding Society's specification for aerospace fusion welding. It's a
        demanding standard, and the discipline it requires, from procedures to inspection to acceptance criteria, carries into every job in the shop.
      </p>

      <figure>
        <Image src={family} alt="The family behind Weld Creations walking together outdoors" width={900} widths={[480, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 90vw, 780px" format="webp" />
      </figure>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Send the drawing, get the finished part.</strong> Welding is our core. Cutting, machining, finishing, passivation and
          specialty processes are handled in-house or through a trusted partner network, so you have one supplier and one purchase order.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Built to your spec.</strong> Your drawing and specification define the job: material, finish, acceptance criteria and documentation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Prototype to production.</strong> We fixture repeat work so the hundredth part matches the approved first article.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Straight answers.</strong> If a part isn't a good fit for us, or a design would be cheaper to build another way, we'll tell you.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we work with</h2>
      <p>
        Pharmaceutical and nutraceutical manufacturers, food and beverage producers, aerospace and defense suppliers, and machine shops and sheet metal
        fabricators that need a dependable welding partner. Our work is concentrated in Los Angeles, Orange and San Bernardino counties, from our shop
        in Glendora.
      </p>
      <p>
        Explore our <a href="/services/">services</a>, the <a href="/materials/">metals we weld</a>, and the <a href="/industries/">industries we serve</a>,
        or download our <a href="/capabilities/">capabilities summary</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
